 1
Create a Function GET_JOB that returns the JOB of an Employee.
Define a session variable TITLE with length 35 characters.
Invoke the function and print the returned JOB.
====================================================================

SQL Command:
------------

sql> SET SERVEROUTPUT ON;

sql> CREATE OR REPLACE FUNCTION GET_JOB
(
     P_EMPNO IN EMP.EMPNO%TYPE
)
RETURN VARCHAR2
IS
     V_JOB EMP.JOB%TYPE;
BEGIN

     SELECT JOB
     INTO V_JOB
     FROM EMP
     WHERE EMPNO=P_EMPNO;

     RETURN V_JOB;

EXCEPTION

     WHEN NO_DATA_FOUND THEN
          RETURN 'EMPLOYEE NOT FOUND';

END;
/

Output:
-------

Function created.


Execute:
--------

sql> VARIABLE TITLE VARCHAR2(35)

sql> EXEC :TITLE:=GET_JOB(7788);

PL/SQL procedure successfully completed.


Print:
------

sql> PRINT TITLE

Output:
-------

TITLE
-----------------------------------
ANALYST


