 4
Create a PL/SQL Function CAL_REVERSE that accepts a string and
returns the reverse of the string.
(Do not use the built-in REVERSE function.)
====================================================================

SQL Command:
------------

sql> CREATE OR REPLACE FUNCTION CAL_REVERSE
(
     P_STR VARCHAR2
)
RETURN VARCHAR2
IS
     V_REV VARCHAR2(200):='';
BEGIN

     FOR I IN REVERSE 1..LENGTH(P_STR)
     LOOP
          V_REV:=V_REV||SUBSTR(P_STR,I,1);
     END LOOP;

     RETURN V_REV;

END;
/

Output:
-------

Function created.


Execute:
--------

sql> SELECT CAL_REVERSE('ORACLE') AS REVERSE_STRING
     FROM DUAL;

Output:
-------

REVERSE_STRING
--------------
ELCARO


